        "evidence": "germ-commutator-q-curvature.lean:50-59: field `parallelogram : obsCommutator δq₁ δq₂ = Fq` and `theorem commutator_eq_curvature (P : ObservationParallelogram R) : obsCommutator P.δq₁ P.δq₂ = P.Fq := P.parallelogram`",
        "notes": "The lean.ref resolves to commutator_eq_curvature, whose body is a verbatim projection of the structure field `parallelogram` whose type IS the theorem's own conclusion (P ⊢ P). The data fields δq₁/δq₂/Fq are not derived through any composition — the identity is assumed as a field and handed back. This is the self-assuming-projection anti-pattern. Restructure so the identity is derived (e.g. carry the two perturbations + a curvature DEFINITION and prove the bracket equals it), or treat the structure as a conjecture carrier. Note agree_iff_flat / curvature_antisymm DO compose fields and are legitimate."
